 "brief": "The base of a small electronics box in PLA (FDM, open side up, layers along Z), screwed to a wall. The wall is the plane z = 0; the box is 100 x 70 mm and 28 mm deep (x = -50 to 50, y = -35 to 35, z = 0 to 28), open at z = 28 where a lid goes on. Two M4 screws go through the floor into the wall at x = -30 and 30, y = 0. A 180 g board (85 x 56 mm) sits on four posts 6 mm across at x = +-38, y = +-23, post tops at z = 8, and the space above it (x = -44 to 44, y = -30 to 30, z = 8 to 28) stays empty for the board and its parts. The outside is a closed 2 mm skin. The box can be knocked: the board's weight at 5 g in any direction, and a cable coming out of the middle of the -y side wall can be tugged with 50 N in any direction. Safety factor 2.",
